            <ArticleTitle>Muscarinic acetylcholine receptor antagonists: SAR and optimization of tyrosine ureas.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>5481-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2008.09.020</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>SAR exploration of multiple regions of a tyrosine urea template led to the identification of very potent muscarinic acetylcholine receptor antagonists such as 10b with good subtype selectivity for M(3) over M(1). The structure-activity relationships (SAR) and optimization of the tyrosine urea series are described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
